WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:01.710
K.

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.400
Tangie Brown.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.500
Jackson made history as the first black female nominee for the Supreme Court.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:11.360
But the tone of her confirmation hearings before the Senate judiciary committee did not stray far from 

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.250
that of other recent nominees.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.860
This is a historic hearing and historic nomination.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.970
And so there is a flavor there that we haven't had in other recent hearings,

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:25.450
but in many ways they are similar as in previous Supreme Court nomination 

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.070
hearings.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:30.040
Senators inquired about Judge Jackson's judicial philosophy,

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.250
the sense you get from her.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.580
She has a very case by case,

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.680
fact by fact approach.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.680
Over the course of my almost decade on 

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.460
the bench,

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.250
I have developed a methodology that I use 

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.360
um in order to ensure that I am ruling impartially 

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.830
and that I am adhering to the limits on my jud 

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.460
judicial authority.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.240
I am acutely aware that as a judge in our 

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:03.960
system,

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.870
I have limited power and um I am 

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:12.260
trying in every case to stay in my lane.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.400
The one thing that was a little bit notable,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.170
she distanced herself from this concept of the living constitution which had been popular in 

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.950
liberal circles for a while,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.110
sort of the antidote to the conservative original meaning of the constitution.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.470
I do not believe that there is a living 

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:34.400
constitution in the sense that it's changing and it's and it's infused with 

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.990
my own policy perspective or uh you know,

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.160
the policy perspective of the day.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.690
Um instead the Supreme Court has made clear that when 

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.450
you're interpreting the constitution,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.820
you're looking at the text at the time of the founding,

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.590
as things started out,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.290
the temperature was low in the room as the hearings went on.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.840
It got a little more charged,

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.100
which is how it has been in past hearings.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:05.340
Some of the most tense exchanges were between Judge Jackson and Republican senators 

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:09.160
questioning her on her sentencing record in child pornography cases.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.340
You are looking at 30,

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:12.900
40,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.060
50 years in prison.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.150
Good,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.130
Good,

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.620
absolutely good.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.150
So you're not going to answer my question?

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:20.710
No,

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.720
I've answered your question and my answer.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.910
You haven't answered my question.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.660
I'm sitting here asking you and your declining to answer.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.400
I have sentenced more than 100 people.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.220
You have eight or nine cases in that chart.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:33.470
Okay,

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.730
Judge you said that before.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.700
These are the eight or nine child porn cases.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.040
I will say to correct the record,

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.250
just say to the judge,

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.510
there's no point in responding.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:40.980
He's going to.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:46.670
It's certainly true that there are cases in which Judge Jackson issued 

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:51.480
sentences to child pornography defendants that were below what sentencing 

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.410
guidelines recommended.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:58.170
But it's also true that the sentencing guidelines on child pornography cases are pretty out of 

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:58.730
date.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.060
There have been calls for them to be updated their,

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:01.350
you know,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.980
been bipartisan agreement that in some cases the guidelines are pretty harsh.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.260
And so if you look at the federal statistics here,

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:13.170
more than two thirds of child pornography defendants are sentenced to below guidelines sentences 

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.930
even though they're all still basically doing prison time.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:20.780
After hours of difficult questioning New Jersey Senator Cory Booker used his 

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.150
allotted time to draw attention back to the historic nature of the hearings.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.460
It's hard for me not to look at you and not see my mom.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.960
I see my ancestors and yours.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:38.130
Nobody's going to steal the joy of that woman in the street or the calls that I'm getting or the 

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:38.650
text.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.850
Nobody's going to steal that joy.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.870
You have earned this spot.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.260
You are worthy.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.560
You are a great american.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.650
There was nothing that happened this week that really changed the trajectory of what's going to happen here.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.320
She came into this hearing likely to be confirmed,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.810
She leaves the hearing likely to be confirmed.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.280
The democrats so long as they stay together,

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.610
have the votes to confirm her.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.060
Even if she doesn't get any Republican votes,

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.850
it would not prevent her from sitting on the Supreme Court.

